<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Stocks to Watch Today - Jan 31.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Stocks to Watch Today - Jan 31.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some Australian stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* MIM Holdings A$1.74 (-.03)</p>
<p>Base metals miner due to report half year results. Analysts expects net loss before abnormals and exchange losses of between A$10 to A$20 million.</p>
<p>* North A$3.92 (+.07)</p>
<p>Mining and forestry group due to report half year results. Analysts expeect a net profit before abnormals of between A$46 to A$54 million for the six months to December 31.</p>
<p>* CSR A$4.42 (-.01)</p>
<p>Building materials group said after trading closed on Thursday it intended to sell its American Aggregates quarrying business for about US$235 million.</p>
<p>* Acacia Resources A$2.25 (+.06)</p>
<p>* Newcrest Mining Ltd A$4.98 (-0.01)</p>
<p>* Normandy A$1.60 (-.01)</p>
<p>* Plutonic A$5.21 (+.06)</p>
<p>* Son of Gwalia A$6.70 (steady)</p>
<p>Bullion price plunges in offshore trade, gold majors in choppy trade in recent days.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
